      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STILTON SHINE (2) gave a start and copped a bump in running when finishing a 6 length sixth (35.19) at this track in a NG. Safe beginner and drawn well close to the inside. Better than last start and worth following up. MARTINI NIGHTS (1) comes into this as a quickest on the card winner last time at Richmond, scoring by 5.5 lengths (35.50). With a good start should be able to take advantage of the rails draw. Must include in calculations. BANDIT SWAGGER (4) recorded a Grade 5 win two back then missed the frame last time at this track, but drawn Box 4 this time where he has won before. Has good speed and can quickly clear the tricky draw. Has the ability and can find best this time. WEST ROCK CASEY (7) should be thereabouts after filling a top-three spot most recently.",
